# After T-708, [defmacro ...] is no longer a keyword — it parses as an implied Call
# to a variable named "defmacro". Since "defmacro" is not defined in prelude,
# this produces an E002 undefined variable error at runtime.
[defmacro my-add [let args] args]
=== error
[E002] undefined variable: defmacro (did you mean the string "defmacro"? Use quotes.) (defined at 3:2-3:10)

=== warn
undefined variable: defmacro at 3:2-3:10
